      "id": "white",
      "name": "Panda",
      "description": "The coat survives in one band round the middle of the horse and nowhere else along it: a bellyband over the shoulder and barrel, wrapping the whole circumference, with all four legs carrying on down from it. Everything else goes white - the head except for the ears, the muzzle and the patches round the eyes, the neck, the back, and the croup and rump behind the band. The tail keeps its colour at the far end of that run, so the horse reads band, then nothing, then tail. The eye patches are a little stylised; muzzle and ear markings are optional. Freckles of coat run along the topline - small, or larger and fawn-like. The edges of the coloured regions are smooth: nothing about Panda is jagged or roaned, and no other marking shows on the white.",
